* A statement r68togas keeps in a note (;[r68: ...], here for the empty string) whose string
* holds a ] before a blank: gastor68 ends the note at the first such ] outside the statement's
* strings, so the round trip gives the statement back whole (it cut it at the string's ]: dc.b
* "[%2d ",$00,""], which r68 refuses).
* fixed: f0be8bc 2026-10-19 gastor68: a note's end outside the statement's strings
* expect text: 5b253264 5d20005b 785d2000 61004e71
 psect t,0,0,0,0,0
 dc.b "[%2d] ",$00,""
 dc.b "[x] ",0,"",'a'
 ends
